IMPORT prelude

-- Georgia individual income tax (O.C.G.A. Title 48, Chapter 7), as amended for taxable years from 2026 by the "Georgia
-- Economic Growth and Tax Relief Act of 2026" (HB 463, Act 465) and with the one-time refund credit of HB 1000 (Act 374,
-- new Code section 48-7-20.4).
--
-- SEAT: the individual taxpayer resident in Georgia for the whole year. "What rate do I pay? What standard deduction and
-- dependent exemption do I get? How much of my pension, my overtime and my tips is left out? How much do I owe? Do I get the
-- one-time refund, and how much?" Provisions addressed to the Department of Revenue or to an employer are encoded as what
-- they mean for that person: the Department must credit my refund; my employer must report my overtime and tips.
--
-- Edition: the Georgia Code is not deposited (the O.C.G.A. public access site puts each section behind a CAPTCHA). What is
-- deposited is the two session laws, as passed by both houses and published by the General Assembly:
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ga-2026-act-465-hb-463-ap.txt (HB 463/AP; strike-through and underlining read from the
--     PDF and recorded in ga-2026-act-465-hb-463-ap.formulas.md)
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ga-2026-act-374-hb-1000-ap.txt (HB 1000, LC 59 0225-EC/AP)
-- Only the text those bills print is encoded. Every other part of 48-7-20, 48-7-26 and 48-7-27 (for example the other
-- subtractions in 48-7-27(a), the additions in 48-7-27(b), and the eligibility tests in 48-7-27(a)(5)(D)) is not deposited
-- and is asked as a fact.
--
-- Federal adjusted gross income and the federal itemized deductions are borrowed federal terms, asked as facts. They are
-- answered by the Internal Revenue Code encoding (subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986/); cross-folder IMPORT is not
-- possible in the stable l4, so NOTES.md names the link.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: nonresidents and part-year residents for the tax itself (their Georgia taxable net income is prorated under
-- 48-7-85, not deposited: `not covered`); taxable years before 2026 (`not covered`); estates and trusts; corporate and
-- partnership rates; the credits repealed by Part IV; Part III (the Revenue Shortfall Reserve).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Georgia individual income tax -- O.C.G.A. 48-7-20, 48-7-26, 48-7-27 as amended by HB 463 (2026), and 48-7-20.4`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `a nonresident or part-year resident's Georgia taxable net income is prorated under Code Section 48-7-85, which is not deposited`
    `taxable years before 2026 are governed by the text before HB 463, which is not deposited`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Facts the person states`

-- 48-7-27(a)(1)(B)(i), (ii): the standard deduction turns on the filing status: "a married couple filing a joint return",
-- or "a single taxpayer, head of household, or married taxpayer filing a separate return".
DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    `single`
    `head of household`
    `married filing separately`
    `married filing jointly`

DECLARE `Residence in Georgia` IS ONE OF
    `resident for the whole taxable year`
    `part-year resident`
    `nonresident`

-- 48-7-27(a)(5)(A)(xiii), (xiv): the retirement income exclusion is "$35,000.00 for each taxpayer meeting the eligibility
-- requirement set forth in division (i) or (ii) of subparagraph (D)" or a larger amount "for each taxpayer meeting the
-- eligibility requirement set forth in division (iii)". Subparagraph (D) is not deposited, so which division the person
-- meets is asked as a fact (NOTES.md finding 6).
DECLARE `Retirement exclusion eligibility` IS ONE OF
    `meets no division of 48-7-27(a)(5)(D)`
    `meets division (i) or (ii) of 48-7-27(a)(5)(D)`
    `meets division (iii) of 48-7-27(a)(5)(D)`

§§ `The annual steps from 2027 and their delays -- 48-7-20(a.1)(1), 48-7-26(b), 48-7-27(a)(1), (1.1)`

-- Each of the four amounts moves "annually beginning on January 1, 2027" until it reaches its final figure: the rate falls
-- by 0.125 to 3.99 percent, the joint standard deduction rises by $750.00 to $36,000.00, the other standard deduction by
-- $375.00 to $18,000.00, the dependent exemption by $125.00 to $6,000.00. Each takes eight steps from its 2026 figure.
-- 48-7-27(a)(1.1)(A): each prospective increase in the standard deduction "shall be delayed by one year for each year that
-- any of the following are true as of December 1" (the Governor's revenue estimate, the prior year's collections, the
-- Revenue Shortfall Reserve). 48-7-26(b) applies "the same delays" to the dependent exemption, and 48-7-20(a.1)(1) delays the
-- rate "by one year for each year that prospective annual reductions in the standard deduction are delayed" (NOTES.md
-- finding 2: "reductions" for increases). The determinations are made and reported by the Office of Planning and Budget
-- ((1.1)(B)): a judgment left to someone else, asked as a fact, the number of December 1 determinations, from 1 December
-- 2026 to 1 December of the year before the taxable year, that found a delay.
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER
      `delayed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the annual steps taken by` `taxable year` `delayed years` IS
    max 0 (`taxable year` MINUS 2026 MINUS `delayed years`)

§§ `48-7-20(a), (a.1)(1) -- the rate`

-- "the tax imposed pursuant to subsection (a) of this Code section shall be 4.99 percent for taxable years beginning on or
-- after January 1, 2026; provided, however, that such rate shall be reduced by 0.125 percent annually beginning on January 1,
-- 2027, until the rate reaches 3.99 percent". "0.125 percent" is read as 0.125 of a percentage point (NOTES.md finding 1).
GIVEN steps IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rate after` steps IS
    max 0.0399 (0.0499 MINUS (0.00125 TIMES steps))

§§ `48-7-27(a)(1) -- the standard deduction or itemized deductions`

-- (B)(i): "In the case of a married couple filing a joint return, $30,000.00; provided, however, that such deduction shall be
-- increased by $750.00 annually beginning on January 1, 2027, until such deduction reaches $36,000.00".
-- (B)(ii): "In the case of a single taxpayer, head of household, or married taxpayer filing a separate return, $15,000.00;
-- provided, however, that such deduction shall be increased by $375.00 annually beginning on January 1, 2027, until such
-- deduction reaches $18,000.00".
GIVEN status IS A `Filing status`
      steps  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the standard deduction for` status `after` steps IS
    IF status EQUALS `married filing jointly`
    THEN min 36000 (30000 PLUS (750 TIMES steps))
    ELSE min 18000 (15000 PLUS (375 TIMES steps))

-- (a)(1): "At the taxpayer's election, either: (A) The sum of all itemized nonbusiness deductions used in computing such
-- taxpayer's federal taxable income; or (B) A standard deduction". The taxpayer elects; the larger is the one that lowers the
-- tax, and that is what the person asks (NOTES.md finding 4: whether (A) needs the taxpayer to have itemized federally).
GIVEN status IS A `Filing status`
      steps  IS A NUMBER
      `federal itemized nonbusiness deductions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the better deduction under 48-7-27(a)(1)` IS
    max `federal itemized nonbusiness deductions` (`the standard deduction for` status `after` steps)

§§ `48-7-26(b) -- the dependent exemption`

-- "a personal exemption in the amount of $5,000.00 for each dependent of such taxpayer; provided, however, that such
-- deduction shall be increased by $125.00 annually beginning on January 1, 2027, until such deduction reaches $6,000.00".
GIVEN steps IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the exemption for each dependent after` steps IS
    min 6000 (5000 PLUS (125 TIMES steps))

§§ `48-7-27(a)(5)(A)(xiii), (xiv) -- the retirement income exclusion`

-- (xiii): "For taxable years beginning on or after January 1, 2012, and ending on or before December 31, 2026, retirement
-- income from any source not to exceed an exclusion amount of $35,000.00 for each taxpayer meeting the eligibility
-- requirement set forth in division (i) or (ii) of subparagraph (D) of this paragraph or an amount of $65,000.00 for each
-- taxpayer meeting the eligibility requirement set forth in division (iii)".
-- (xiv): "For taxable years beginning on or after January 1, 2027", $35,000.00 or $70,000.00 on the same tests.
-- The exclusion is "for each taxpayer": on a joint return each spouse has their own (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER
      eligibility    IS A `Retirement exclusion eligibility`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the retirement exclusion cap for` `taxable year` eligibility IS
    CONSIDER eligibility
    WHEN `meets no division of 48-7-27(a)(5)(D)`     THEN 0
    WHEN `meets division (i) or (ii) of 48-7-27(a)(5)(D)` THEN 35000
    WHEN `meets division (iii) of 48-7-27(a)(5)(D)`  THEN IF `taxable year` AT MOST 2026 THEN 65000 ELSE 70000

GIVEN `taxable year`      IS A NUMBER
      eligibility         IS A `Retirement exclusion eligibility`
      `retirement income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the retirement income excluded for one taxpayer` IS
    min (max 0 `retirement income`) (`the retirement exclusion cap for` `taxable year` eligibility)

§§ `48-7-27(a)(16), (17) -- overtime and cash tips`

-- (16)(A): "For all taxable years beginning on or after January 1, 2026, and ending on December 31, 2028, any amount of
-- qualified overtime compensation, as such term is defined in Section 225 of the Internal Revenue Code, up to $1,750.00
-- received by a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage." (E): the paragraph "shall stand repealed and reserved on December
-- 31, 2028". "Qualified overtime compensation" is a borrowed federal term, asked as a fact.
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER
      `I am a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `qualified overtime compensation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the overtime subtracted` IS
    IF     `taxable year` AT LEAST 2026
       AND `taxable year` AT MOST 2028
       AND `I am a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage`
    THEN min 1750 (max 0 `qualified overtime compensation`)
    ELSE 0

-- (17)(A): "For all taxable years beginning on or after January 1, 2026, any amount up to $1,750.00 received in cash tips."
-- (D)(i) defines "cash tips" (an occupation that customarily and regularly receives tips, paid voluntarily, not negotiated,
-- set by the payor); asked as a fact. (E): "This paragraph shall stand repealed and reserved on December 31, 2028" (NOTES.md
-- finding 3: (A) has no end year of its own, but (E) repeals it, so nothing is subtracted after 2028).
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER
      `cash tips` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cash tips subtracted` IS
    IF `taxable year` AT LEAST 2026 AND `taxable year` AT MOST 2028
    THEN min 1750 (max 0 `cash tips`)
    ELSE 0

-- (16)(C), (17)(B): "each employer shall submit to the department ... the total amount of qualified overtime compensation
-- [cash tips] ... The data shall be provided monthly or quarterly and shall be due no later than the due date for the
-- corresponding monthly or quarterly withholding tax returns, except that such data may be provided at the end of the year
-- for the 2026 tax year." A duty on the employer, encoded for what it means to the employee: the employer must report.
-- The time to the withholding return's due date is not deposited and is an input, in days.
DECLARE `Georgia tax party` IS ONE OF
    `the taxpayer`
    `my employer`
    `the Department of Revenue`

DECLARE `Georgia tax act` IS ONE OF
    `report the overtime and cash tips data for the period to the department`
    `file my 2025 Georgia income tax return`
    `credit me with the one-time refund` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the refund less any outstanding liability, electronically or by check as my 2025 return instructs`

GIVEN `days to the due date of the withholding return for the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Georgia tax party` `Georgia tax act`
`48-7-27(a)(16)(C), (17)(B) -- my employer must report overtime and tips with each withholding return` MEANS
    PARTY `my employer`
    MUST  `report the overtime and cash tips data for the period to the department`
    WITHIN `days to the due date of the withholding return for the period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `my employer` BECAUSE "48-7-27(a)(16)(C), (17)(B): the employer's overtime and tips data are due no later than the due date for the corresponding monthly or quarterly withholding tax return"

§§ `Georgia taxable net income and the tax -- 48-7-27(a), 48-7-20(a)`

-- 48-7-27(a): "Georgia taxable net income of an individual shall be the taxpayer's federal adjusted gross income ... less"
-- the paragraphs of subsection (a). Only (1), (5)(A)(xiii)-(xiv), (16) and (17) are deposited. The other subtractions of
-- subsection (a), and the additions of subsection (b), are taken as one net figure the person states. 48-7-26(b) allows the
-- dependent exemption "as a deduction in computing his or her Georgia taxable income".
-- 48-7-20(a): "A tax is imposed upon every resident of this state with respect to the Georgia taxable net income of the
-- taxpayer as defined in Code Section 48-7-27." No tax on a negative figure: the tax is on income, so a negative Georgia
-- taxable net income gives nil (NOTES.md finding 7).
DECLARE `Return facts` HAS
    `taxable year` IS A NUMBER
    `delayed years` IS A NUMBER
    residence IS A `Residence in Georgia`
    status IS A `Filing status`
    `federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
    `federal itemized nonbusiness deductions` IS A NUMBER
    `dependents` IS A NUMBER
    `my retirement exclusion eligibility` IS A `Retirement exclusion eligibility`
    `my retirement income` IS A NUMBER
    `my spouse's retirement exclusion eligibility` IS A `Retirement exclusion eligibility`
    `my spouse's retirement income` IS A NUMBER
    `I am a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my qualified overtime compensation` IS A NUMBER
    `my spouse is a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my spouse's qualified overtime compensation` IS A NUMBER
    `my cash tips` IS A NUMBER
    `my spouse's cash tips` IS A NUMBER
    `other subtractions less additions` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the steps for` r IS `the annual steps taken by` (r's `taxable year`) (r's `delayed years`)

GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the return is joint` IF r's status EQUALS `married filing jointly`

GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the subtractions for` r IS
        `the better deduction under 48-7-27(a)(1)` (r's status) (`the steps for` r) (r's `federal itemized nonbusiness deductions`)
    PLUS (r's `dependents` TIMES `the exemption for each dependent after` (`the steps for` r))
    PLUS `the retirement income excluded for one taxpayer` (r's `taxable year`) (r's `my retirement exclusion eligibility`) (r's `my retirement income`)
    PLUS `the overtime subtracted` (r's `taxable year`) (r's `I am a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage`) (r's `my qualified overtime compensation`)
    PLUS `the cash tips subtracted` (r's `taxable year`) (r's `my cash tips`)
    PLUS `the spouse's subtractions for` r
    PLUS r's `other subtractions less additions`
    WHERE
        `the spouse's subtractions for` x MEANS
            IF `the return is joint` x
            THEN     `the retirement income excluded for one taxpayer` (x's `taxable year`) (x's `my spouse's retirement exclusion eligibility`) (x's `my spouse's retirement income`)
                PLUS `the overtime subtracted` (x's `taxable year`) (x's `my spouse is a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage`) (x's `my spouse's qualified overtime compensation`)
                PLUS `the cash tips subtracted` (x's `taxable year`) (x's `my spouse's cash tips`)
            ELSE 0

GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `Georgia taxable net income for` r IS
    IF r's `taxable year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `not covered` `taxable years before 2026 are governed by the text before HB 463, which is not deposited`
    ELSE IF NOT (r's residence EQUALS `resident for the whole taxable year`)
         THEN `not covered` `a nonresident or part-year resident's Georgia taxable net income is prorated under Code Section 48-7-85, which is not deposited`
         ELSE `answered` (r's `federal adjusted gross income` MINUS `the subtractions for` r)

GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `Georgia income tax for` r IS
    CONSIDER `Georgia taxable net income for` r
    WHEN `answered` income THEN `answered` (max 0 income TIMES `the rate after` (`the steps for` r))
    WHEN `not covered` why THEN `not covered` why

§§ `48-7-20.4 -- the one-time refund credit (HB 1000)`

-- (a): "'qualified taxpayer' means an individual taxpayer who filed an individual income tax return for both the 2024 and
-- 2025 taxable years by the due date for filing the income tax return for the 2025 taxable year, including any extensions
-- which have been granted. Such term shall: (1) Not include any: (A) Nonresident alien individual; (B) Individual who was
-- claimed as a dependent by another taxpayer for federal or Georgia income tax purposes for the 2024 taxable year; or (C)
-- Estate or trust; and (2) Include any individual taxpayer excluded solely due to subparagraph (B) ... provided that such
-- individual had earned income for the 2024 taxable year."
GIVEN `I filed my 2024 and 2025 returns by the 2025 due date, with extensions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a nonresident alien individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was claimed as a dependent for 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had earned income for 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a qualified taxpayer under 48-7-20.4(a)` IF
        `I filed my 2024 and 2025 returns by the 2025 due date, with extensions`
    AND (NOT `I am a nonresident alien individual`)
    AND (    (NOT `I was claimed as a dependent for 2024`)
         OR  `I had earned income for 2024`)

-- (b)(1): "a one-time refund amount equal to the lesser of: (A) The qualified taxpayer's 2024 individual income tax liability
-- as properly reported on Line 16 of the 2024 Georgia Form 500 or Line 4 of the 2024 Georgia Form 500EZ; or (B) An amount,
-- which is based on such taxpayer's filing status for the 2024 taxable year, equal to: (i) ... single taxpayer or a married
-- taxpayer filing a separate return, $250.00; (ii) ... head of household, $375.00; or (iii) ... married couple filing a
-- joint return, $500.00."
-- (b)(2): for "any taxable nonresident or part-year resident whose tax was prorated as provided by Code Section 48-7-85, the
-- amount ... shall be prorated based on the ratio of income taxable to Georgia as properly reported on Schedule 3, Line 9".
-- (b)(3): never "greater than the taxpayer's individual income tax liability" for 2024.
GIVEN status IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 48-7-20.4(b)(1)(B) amount for` status IS
    CONSIDER status
    WHEN `single`                   THEN 250
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN 250
    WHEN `head of household`        THEN 375
    WHEN `married filing jointly`   THEN 500

GIVEN `my 2024 Georgia income tax liability` IS A NUMBER
      `my 2024 filing status` IS A `Filing status`
      `my 2024 tax was prorated under 48-7-85` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my Schedule 3 line 9 ratio` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the one-time refund amount` IS
    min (max 0 `my 2024 Georgia income tax liability`) `the prorated amount`
    WHERE
        `the lesser amount` MEANS min (max 0 `my 2024 Georgia income tax liability`) (`the 48-7-20.4(b)(1)(B) amount for` `my 2024 filing status`)
        `the prorated amount` MEANS
            IF `my 2024 tax was prorated under 48-7-85`
            THEN `the lesser amount` TIMES `my Schedule 3 line 9 ratio`
            ELSE `the lesser amount`

-- (b)(1): "Once a qualified taxpayer files an individual income tax return for the 2025 taxable year, the department shall
-- automatically credit such qualified taxpayer with a one-time refund amount". No time is set for the Department.
-- (d): the refund "shall be either electronically transmitted or sent by check to such taxpayer, based on the taxpayer's
-- refund instructions, if any, as indicated on the taxpayer's income tax return for the 2025 taxable year, provided that such
-- refund shall first be credited against any outstanding liability". (e): no interest; (f): subject to setoff debt collection.
-- Filing by the 2025 due date is part of being a qualified taxpayer ((a)); filing late is no breach, it just earns no credit.
GIVEN `days to the 2025 return due date, with extensions` IS A NUMBER
      `my one-time refund amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Georgia tax party` `Georgia tax act`
`48-7-20.4(a), (b)(1), (d) -- once I file my 2025 return in time, the Department must credit and pay my one-time refund` MEANS
    PARTY `the taxpayer`
    DO    `file my 2025 Georgia income tax return`
    WITHIN `days to the 2025 return due date, with extensions`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `the Department of Revenue`
        MUST  `credit me with the one-time refund` (EXACTLY `my one-time refund amount`)
        HENCE (
            PARTY `the Department of Revenue`
            MUST  `pay the refund less any outstanding liability, electronically or by check as my 2025 return instructs`))
    LEST  FULFILLED

§ `Questions for the taxpayer`

§§ `The rate and the deductions`

@export What is the Georgia individual income tax rate for my taxable year (O.C.G.A. 48-7-20(a.1))?
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year your tax return is for (2026 or later)
      `delayed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the Office of Planning and Budget's December 1 determinations, from 1 December 2026 to 1 December of the year before your taxable year, found a delay under 48-7-27(a)(1.1) (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my Georgia income tax rate` IS
    IF `taxable year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `not covered` `taxable years before 2026 are governed by the text before HB 463, which is not deposited`
    ELSE `answered` (`the rate after` (`the annual steps taken by` `taxable year` `delayed years`))

@export What Georgia standard deduction can I take (O.C.G.A. 48-7-27(a)(1)(B))?
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year your tax return is for (2026 or later)
      `delayed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many December 1 determinations since 2026 found a delay under 48-7-27(a)(1.1) (0 if none)
      status IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, head of household, married filing separately, or married filing jointly
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my Georgia standard deduction` IS
    IF `taxable year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `not covered` `taxable years before 2026 are governed by the text before HB 463, which is not deposited`
    ELSE `answered` (`the standard deduction for` status `after` (`the annual steps taken by` `taxable year` `delayed years`))

@export Should I take the Georgia standard deduction or my federal itemized deductions, and how much is it (O.C.G.A. 48-7-27(a)(1))?
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year your tax return is for (2026 or later)
      `delayed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many December 1 determinations since 2026 found a delay under 48-7-27(a)(1.1) (0 if none)
      status IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status
      `federal itemized nonbusiness deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the itemized nonbusiness deductions used in computing your federal taxable income, in dollars (0 if you do not itemize)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `Which Georgia deduction is better for me` IS
    IF `taxable year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `not covered` `taxable years before 2026 are governed by the text before HB 463, which is not deposited`
    ELSE `answered` (`the better deduction under 48-7-27(a)(1)` status (`the annual steps taken by` `taxable year` `delayed years`) `federal itemized nonbusiness deductions`)

@export How much is my Georgia exemption for each dependent (O.C.G.A. 48-7-26(b))?
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year your tax return is for (2026 or later)
      `delayed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many December 1 determinations since 2026 found a delay under 48-7-27(a)(1.1) (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my Georgia dependent exemption` IS
    IF `taxable year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `not covered` `taxable years before 2026 are governed by the text before HB 463, which is not deposited`
    ELSE `answered` (`the exemption for each dependent after` (`the annual steps taken by` `taxable year` `delayed years`))

§§ `Retirement income, overtime and tips`

@export How much of my retirement income is left out of my Georgia taxable income (O.C.G.A. 48-7-27(a)(5)(A)(xiii), (xiv))?
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year your tax return is for (2026 or later)
      eligibility IS A `Retirement exclusion eligibility` @desc Which eligibility division of 48-7-27(a)(5)(D) you meet: none, division (i) or (ii), or division (iii) (the larger exclusion)
      `retirement income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your retirement income from any source included in your federal adjusted gross income, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my retirement income is excluded` IS
    IF `taxable year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `not covered` `taxable years before 2026 are governed by the text before HB 463, which is not deposited`
    ELSE `answered` (`the retirement income excluded for one taxpayer` `taxable year` eligibility `retirement income`)

@export How much of my overtime pay is left out of my Georgia taxable income (O.C.G.A. 48-7-27(a)(16))?
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year your tax return is for
      `full-time hourly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage
      `qualified overtime compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc Your qualified overtime compensation as defined in section 225 of the Internal Revenue Code, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my overtime is excluded` IS
    `the overtime subtracted` `taxable year` `full-time hourly` `qualified overtime compensation`

@export How much of my cash tips is left out of my Georgia taxable income (O.C.G.A. 48-7-27(a)(17))?
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year your tax return is for
      `cash tips` IS A NUMBER @desc Cash tips you received in an occupation that customarily and regularly receives tips (paid voluntarily, not negotiated, set by the customer), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my cash tips is excluded` IS
    `the cash tips subtracted` `taxable year` `cash tips`

§§ `What I owe`

@export How much Georgia individual income tax do I owe for the year (O.C.G.A. 48-7-20, 48-7-26, 48-7-27)?
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year your tax return is for (2026 or later)
      `delayed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many December 1 determinations since 2026 found a delay under 48-7-27(a)(1.1) (0 if none)
      residence IS A `Residence in Georgia` @desc Whether you were a Georgia resident for the whole year, a part-year resident, or a nonresident
      status IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status
      `federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income (joint if you file jointly), in dollars
      `federal itemized nonbusiness deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal itemized nonbusiness deductions, in dollars (0 if you do not itemize)
      dependents IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents you claim
      `my retirement exclusion eligibility` IS A `Retirement exclusion eligibility` @desc Which eligibility division of 48-7-27(a)(5)(D) you meet for the retirement exclusion
      `my retirement income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your retirement income included in federal adjusted gross income, in dollars
      `my spouse's retirement exclusion eligibility` IS A `Retirement exclusion eligibility` @desc On a joint return, which division your spouse meets (otherwise none)
      `my spouse's retirement income` IS A NUMBER @desc On a joint return, your spouse's retirement income included in federal adjusted gross income (otherwise 0)
      `I am full-time hourly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage
      `my qualified overtime compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc Your qualified overtime compensation (IRC s 225), in dollars
      `my spouse is full-time hourly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a joint return, whether your spouse is a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage
      `my spouse's qualified overtime compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc On a joint return, your spouse's qualified overtime compensation, in dollars
      `my cash tips` IS A NUMBER @desc Your cash tips, in dollars
      `my spouse's cash tips` IS A NUMBER @desc On a joint return, your spouse's cash tips, in dollars
      `other subtractions less additions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other Georgia subtractions under 48-7-27(a) less any additions under 48-7-27(b), in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `How much Georgia income tax do I owe` IS
    `Georgia income tax for` (`Return facts` WITH
        `taxable year` IS `taxable year`
        `delayed years` IS `delayed years`
        residence IS residence
        status IS status
        `federal adjusted gross income` IS `federal adjusted gross income`
        `federal itemized nonbusiness deductions` IS `federal itemized nonbusiness deductions`
        `dependents` IS dependents
        `my retirement exclusion eligibility` IS `my retirement exclusion eligibility`
        `my retirement income` IS `my retirement income`
        `my spouse's retirement exclusion eligibility` IS `my spouse's retirement exclusion eligibility`
        `my spouse's retirement income` IS `my spouse's retirement income`
        `I am a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage` IS `I am full-time hourly`
        `my qualified overtime compensation` IS `my qualified overtime compensation`
        `my spouse is a full-time employee paid by an hourly wage` IS `my spouse is full-time hourly`
        `my spouse's qualified overtime compensation` IS `my spouse's qualified overtime compensation`
        `my cash tips` IS `my cash tips`
        `my spouse's cash tips` IS `my spouse's cash tips`
        `other subtractions less additions` IS `other subtractions less additions`)

§§ `The one-time refund (HB 1000)`

@export Am I a qualified taxpayer for Georgia's one-time income tax refund (O.C.G.A. 48-7-20.4(a))?
GIVEN `filed both returns in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you filed Georgia individual income tax returns for both 2024 and 2025 by the due date for the 2025 return, including any extension granted
      `nonresident alien` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a nonresident alien individual
      `claimed as a dependent for 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another taxpayer claimed you as a dependent for federal or Georgia income tax purposes for 2024
      `earned income for 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had earned income for 2024
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a qualified taxpayer for the one-time refund` IF
    `I am a qualified taxpayer under 48-7-20.4(a)` `filed both returns in time` `nonresident alien` `claimed as a dependent for 2024` `earned income for 2024`

@export How much is my Georgia one-time income tax refund (O.C.G.A. 48-7-20.4(b))?
GIVEN `qualified taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a qualified taxpayer under 48-7-20.4(a) (see the question above)
      `2024 liability` IS A NUMBER @desc Your 2024 Georgia individual income tax liability as properly reported on Line 16 of Form 500 or Line 4 of Form 500EZ, in dollars
      `2024 filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status for 2024
      `prorated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your 2024 tax was prorated as a nonresident or part-year resident under 48-7-85
      `ratio` IS A NUMBER @desc If prorated, the ratio of income taxable to Georgia on Schedule 3, Line 9 of your 2024 Form 500, as a fraction (for example 0.5); otherwise 1
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my one-time refund` IS
    IF `qualified taxpayer`
    THEN `the one-time refund amount` `2024 liability` `2024 filing status` `prorated` `ratio`
    ELSE 0
